SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Villa Albertine: 2028 Exploratory Residencies i
 n the United States (one to three months\, about USD 3\,300 per month plus
  travel and housing\; French partner required)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 21 Jan 2027 at 23:59 CET.\n\nVilla Albertine\, the Frenc
 h Embassy's residency institution in the United States\, will host around 
 fifty exploratory residencies between January and December 2028 for artist
 s\, thinkers and cultural professionals whose projects can only take shape
  through a stay in the US.\n\nOrganisation: Villa Albertine (Embassy of Fr
 ance in the United States)\nLocation: Cities across the United States\, us
 ually one city per residency\, with a few roving residencies. Open to any 
 nationality and to French and non-French speakers\, but every application 
 needs a letter of support from a partner organisation based in France. Min
 imum age 21.\nAward: Residency stipend of about USD 110 per day (roughly U
 SD 3\,300 per month\, adjusted to the city)\, paid as a lump sum. Internat
 ional travel (and domestic travel for roving residencies)\, accommodation\
 , insurance and\, where needed\, a rental car are covered separately. No a
 pplication fee stated.\nDuration: 1 to 3 months between January and Decemb
 er 2028\n\nMore: https://villa-albertine.org/va/professionals/appel-a-cand
 idatures-de-la-villa-albertine-residences-2028/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://villa-albertine.org/va/professionals/appel-a-candidatures-de-la
 -villa-albertine-residences-2028/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cities across the United States\, usually one city per residency\,
  with a few roving residencies. Open to any nationality and to French and 
 non-French speakers\, but every application needs a letter of support from
  a partner organisation based in France. Minimum age 21.
END:VEVENT
